    title: "Daily Practice",
    content: "Guard against these common distortions of the gospel this week:\n\n1. **Examine your motives for obedience.** Choose one spiritual practice you maintain regularly — Sabbath observance, tithing, dietary choices, prayer habits. Ask yourself honestly: \"Am I doing this because I love God, or because I fear rejection?\" If fear is the dominant motive, bring it to God and ask Him to replace it with the \"faith working through love\" that Paul describes.\n\n2. **Let faith produce a visible work.** James insists that living faith is active. Identify one concrete act of service you can perform this week that costs you something — time, money, comfort, or pride. Do it without announcing it. Let the action be the evidence of the faith you profess.\n\n3. **Remember your baptism.** If you have been baptized, recall the moment and what it signified. Read Romans 6:1-4 and reflect: \"I died with Christ. I was buried with Him. I was raised to walk in new life.\" If patterns from the old life are reasserting themselves, bring them under the authority of what happened at that water.",
